module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_red_control_that_was_never_red_on_any_tree_reads_as_a_control

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_red_control_that_was_never_red_on_any_tree_reads_as_a_control: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_red_control_that_was_never_red_on_any_tree_reads_as_a_control" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "**a red control that was never red on any tree reads as a control** (INVALID STATE: a roadmap row's red_control names claims that exist and that PASS on BOTH sides of the change the row asks for, and beside them a sentence promising an instrument -- 'an instrument shows no subtree re-walk on that path' -- while no counter for that instrument exists anywhere in the corpus. HARM: the row reads closed. A reader greps the named module, finds green claims, and cannot tell that they certify invariance ACROSS the change rather than sensitivity TO it; the promise beside them supplies the half the claims do not, and the two halves together look like a control. A control never observed red on any tree is not a control, which is why gunbc.design_ruling::executed_red_control_names_its_failing_commit makes red_at data rather than prose).",

    "SPECIMEN (2026-11-25, planning eager-bear-102, node v1-parse-allocator-carried, identity rn_BS0YK7QAA67P73F6YYGZRTGXJ3). At main 5611ac47e730 its red_control read: 'Allocated ids are identical before and after on a fixture with a long operator chain, and an instrument shows no subtree re-walk on that path.' The first clause is met by eight claims in v1.tests.claim.parse_allocator_postcondition_test: `long_left_associated_chain_postcondition`, `parameters_arguments_statements_postcondition`, `chain40_transport_identity_matches_predeletion_golden`, `chain200_transport_identity_matches_predeletion_golden`, `folds_transport_identity_matches_predeletion_golden`, `chain40_transport_content_association_matches_predeletion_golden`, `chain200_transport_content_association_matches_predeletion_golden` and `folds_transport_content_association_matches_predeletion_golden`. The second has no witness: a case-insensitive grep of that module for rewalk, re-walk, instrument, occurrence_allocator_after, eval_steps or counter returns 0 matches, and occurrence_allocator_after_node has 0 hits in any claim module at main against 14 hits in src/v1/02_parse.dag. The eight claims are byte-identical between main and the implementation head 9eab2a2882a5 (module sha256 eb47ade80d3ba039ec4d4c551af3b841963a304ec4cb88b85610d49640e7dfdf, git diff --stat prints nothing) and all eight PASS at both trees, so none was ever red with respect to the deletion. The module's own header says the goldens were captured with the recovery walks present and that the two runs produced byte-identical digest lines: they certify allocator-identity invariance, which that same row puts in out_of_scope.",

    "MEASURED THE SAME DAY, so this row is not a claim that nothing was saved. The deletion is real (src/v1/02_parse.dag 7132 lines to 7006, occurrence_allocator_after_node 14 hits to 0, nine functions gone) and the saving is real and chain-shaped. One claim_batch binary whose sha256 is a53867a57b587969e494b3989708ba741da2ad4ee7f316fb2a561a819e3afc6d (a binary hash, not a commit -- and NOT a released instrument: its source src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs is deleted at main by ad5c67a316f6, `git cat-file -e origin/main:src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_batch.rs` rc=128, and the binary survives as exactly two scratch copies on srv1, so this leg is a HISTORICAL OBSERVATION, not an executable gate. Wrong-case confirmation 2026-11-27 on the maintained `gunbc test` route at 2edbf0391f6fc0cb1c80ab1045c40a55c901948e, WHICH WAS A MAIN TIP. An earlier revision of this receipt labelled that commit a scratch merge of main into the change`s branch and NOT a main tip; THAT LABEL WAS FALSE and the correction is recorded here rather than written over. Measured 2026-11-27: gh api repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/pulls/17182 prints merged=true, merged_at 2026-11-27T05:44:41Z, base=main and merge_commit_sha 2edbf0391f6fc0cb1c80ab1045c40a55c901948e; the commit has ONE parent, ebc880f930e458c2fb998e1eb1ce71dc3bc1a4a6, which was main at 05:30:49Z; `git rev-list --first-parent origin/main` contains it (grep -c = 1); and GitHub lists it among sha=main`s commits between 05:00Z and 07:00Z. This repository lands every pull as a single-parent squash-merge commit on main, so one parent is never evidence that a commit is off main -- that is the inference error this row type exists to catch. main stood at it from 2026-11-27T05:44:40Z until 6be13eea95b1 replaced it at 05:58:28Z. eval_steps 418389 over B, gunbc sha256 1fe5d8748de2d0a8947721cedcf32ea2ccf42c34e2472631cb80ac575a3405d1 built in that arm`s own worktree, rc=0.), one command line, only the tree varying, srv1 under heavy-slot, trees checked out clean at 5611ac47e730427f6d19f9bf765c561b01c36de7 and 9eab2a2882a56571220b0d0b5d8d7864b7d8aafd: chain200 identity eval_steps 418120 to 396027, chain200 content association 640998 to 618905, chain40 identity 88689 to 84196, chain40 content association 101218 to 96725, folds identity 48536 to 44896, folds content association 52937 to 49297. Every delta tracks chain length -- -22093 at length 200 and -4493 at length 40, a ratio of 4.9 for a 5x chain, which is LINEAR at these sizes. The row's `displaced_cost` now carries the quadratic as a BET, neither deleted nor promoted, so what this table settles is the saving and what it leaves open is the exponent -- open until a counter can attribute steps to a walk. WHAT THAT TABLE IS NOT: a measurement with no verdict cannot gate. No claim asserted those numbers, nothing went red on them, and a differential quoted into prose is review evidence, not a control. THE PAIR NOW EXISTS ON THE MAINTAINED ROUTE, AND THAT IS WHAT THIS FAILURE-MODE ROW WAS FOR: wrong case 418389 read TWICE, at 2edbf0391f6fc0cb1c80ab1045c40a55c901948e (built-and-run gunbc sha256 1fe5d8748de2d0a8947721cedcf32ea2ccf42c34e2472631cb80ac575a3405d1, rc=0) and at main tip b07fd2aac7231a3064abf41453f851a9f030d0f5 (built-and-run gunbc sha256 e519d98f63f07c20e181e5af529a767e5e9db443dae5d199965471aa76b468ed, rc=0), over 407000; accepting case 396296 at 3f161b359078b4e93304598ab48b8a71319f7451, a tree carrying the deletion AND the route (built-and-run gunbc sha256 6479b7193718275872bdd9b1c3796471d9acd37ed08dfe46394317bf22bc92e5, rc=0), under 407000. 418389 - 396296 = 22093, equal to the claim_batch delta 418120 - 396027 = 22093, and the maintained route sits a constant 269 steps above the claim_batch route on BOTH arms -- which is why the bound is route-independent and why no figure here may be swapped for another. The accepting side is n=1 build with n=2 runs agreeing exactly at 396296: the first acquired at load 48.37, above the lane`s load-45 bar, kept labelled superseded rather than deleted; the second at 40.67 against LOAD_BAR=45 with the guard's own source lines and refusal in the log, no cargo line in the leg, claim log sha256 774e8b36403d5a74e4860b4b8af4c2b1e502ec71506eb3b008afd97df3e8defc (run 7216061692, which keeps the superseded leg labelled rather than deleted). The lesson the row type carries stands: a control that was never observed red on any tree is not a control, and eight green claims that were green before the change and green after it certify invariance, not the change.",

    "WHAT CLOSES IT, AND WHY IT IS NOT WRITTEN HERE. The discriminating control available today is a step BUDGET: the row now carries B = 407000 eval steps on the chain-200 identity claim, with the pair above as its provenance, so the wrong case is refused (418120 over B) and the right case accepted (396027 under B) by the same reading the floor already uses for budgets (`claim_eval_step_standing` in v2.workflow.required_floor, EvalStepsOverBudget over EvalStepsWithinBudget). A budget refuses on COST and cannot name a CAUSE. The claim that would name the cause asserts a ZERO count of recovery walks on the left-operand path, and a zero-count claim needs a COUNTER: no counter over occurrence_allocator_after_node exists in the emitted host or in any claim module, and building one is implementation, so it belongs to a future node and not to a row edit. TRIGGER for this class: the re-walk returning on the left-operand path -- a producer stops publishing its minted identities, or the carried allocator is dropped and a recovery scan is re-added. The budget sees that only as a cost increase, and only if the fixture reaches the path; the bound is also crossable by legitimate work, whose remedy is a fresh pair measured at two named shas on a named binary, never a silent widening of the literal.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE. When a red_control names an instrument, grep the corpus for the counter it would read: 0 hits means the sentence is prose. Then ask whether the named claims were ever RED. Byte-identical at both trees and green at both means they certify invariance, not sensitivity -- the change could be reverted and every one of them would still pass. A row whose control cannot go red is an open row, whatever its fields assert.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
